module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.FrobeniusColimitVectorBundleGroupoidFibrationStack
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.FrobeniusColimitVectorBundleGroupoidFullSubcategory
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.HTopology.BigHOverZariskiPrecoverage

/-!
# Condition (1) of Stacks 0EX9 for Stacks Tag 0EXE, tested on the generating Zariski families

Condition (1) of Stacks 0EX9 for the category fibred in groupoids of Stacks Tag 0EXE is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.IsZariskiStackInGroupoids`, a statement about *every* covering sieve
of `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiTopology`. That topology is only *generated* by the Zariski
families of the site, so the condition is not the conjunction of the stack conditions for those
families; passing from the generators to the generated topology is
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage`, whose hypotheses on the precoverage are
now available from
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/HTopology/BigHOverZariskiPrecoverage.lean`.

This file runs that reduction and chains it with the two steps already in the development — the
bridge from the pseudofunctor to the structure functor and the descent of the stack condition to
the finite locally free full subcategory — so that condition (1) is reduced to a statement about
single Zariski families of the site.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isStack_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor_zariski`: **the
  pseudofunctor in groupoids of Stacks Tag 0EXE is a stack for the Zariski topology of the big h
  category over `S` as soon as it is a stack for every Zariski family of the site.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isZariskiStackInGroupoids_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration_of_families`:
  **condition (1) of Stacks 0EX9 for Stacks Tag 0EXE, reduced to the Zariski families of the
  site**: it holds as soon as, for every Zariski family, the pseudofunctor of *all*
  Frobenius-colimit modules is a stack for that family and finite local freeness is detected on
  it.

## Implementation notes

The reduction is run on the pseudofunctor in groupoids rather than on the structure functor,
because `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage` is a statement about
pseudofunctors;
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZariskiStackInGroupoids_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration` then crosses
to the structure functor, which is where condition (1) lives.

`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage` hands out an arbitrary presieve of the
precoverage, while `AlgebraicGeometry.isStackFor_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor` is
stated for a `CategoryTheory.Presieve.ofArrows` family.
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.exists_eq_ofArrows` closes that gap, and it is the reason the index
universe of the full-subcategory step had to be widened: the family it produces for the big h
category over `S` is indexed by a type of `Type (u + 1)`, not of `Type u`.

Neither of the two per-family hypotheses is discharged here. `hR` is Zariski descent for sheaves
of `colim_F 𝒪_U`-modules, for which the development has the separatedness half
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceRestriction.overFunctor_map_injective`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.frobeniusColimitPullback_map_injective`) but not the effectivity half. `hP` is
the locality of finite local freeness along the family; for a general family of the big h site it
is not expected, and it is stated per family for that reason.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EXE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EX9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EX9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor Opposite
open Stacks.Frobenius

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

variable (B : BigHSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S) (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
  (hpS : IsInCharacteristic S p)

include hpS

/-- **The pseudofunctor in groupoids of Stacks Tag 0EXE is a stack for the Zariski topology of
the big h category over `S` as soon as it is a stack for every Zariski family of the site.**

The Zariski topology of the site is generated by the Zariski families, and
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage` is what turns a family-wise stack condition
into one for every covering sieve of the generated topology. Its hypotheses on the precoverage
are `AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage_hasIsos`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage_isStableUnderBaseChange` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage_isStableUnderComposition`, and the pullbacks of
the site are `AlgebraicGeometry.hasPullbacks_bigHOver`. -/
theorem isStack_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor_zariski
    (h : ∀ (U : BigHOver B S hS) (R : Presieve U),
      R ∈ (BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage B S hS).coverings U →
        (frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor B S hS p hpS).IsStackFor R) :
    (frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor B S hS p hpS).IsStack
      (BigHOver.zariskiTopology B S hS) :=
  Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage (J := BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage B S hS) h

/-- **Condition (1) of Stacks 0EX9 for the category fibred in groupoids of Stacks Tag 0EXE,
reduced to the Zariski families of the site.**

For every Zariski family `f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U` of the big h category over `S`, two inputs are asked
for: that the pseudofunctor of *all* sheaves of `colim_F 𝒪_U`-modules is a stack for the family,
and that finite local freeness of a sheaf of `colim_F 𝒪_U`-modules is detected by its scalar
extensions along the family. Neither is proved here.

The chain is `AlgebraicGeometry.isStackFor_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor` per
family, then `AlgebraicGeometry.isStack_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor_zariski` to
the whole topology, then
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZariskiStackInGroupoids_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration` to the
structure functor. -/
theorem isZariskiStackInGroupoids_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration_of_families
    (hP : ∀ {ι : Type (u + 1)} {U : BigHOver B S hS} {X : ι → BigHOver B S hS}
      (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U), Presieve.ofArrows X f ∈
        (BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage B S hS).coverings U →
      ∀ M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (bigHFrobeniusColimitRingSheaf B S hS p hpS U),
        (∀ i, SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u}
            ((bigHFrobeniusColimitPullback B S hS p hpS (f i).op).obj M)) →
          SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} M)
    (hR : ∀ {ι : Type (u + 1)} {U : BigHOver B S hS} {X : ι → BigHOver B S hS}
      (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ U), Presieve.ofArrows X f ∈
        (BigHOver.zariskiPrecoverage B S hS).coverings U →
      (frobeniusColimitModulePseudofunctor B S hS p hpS).IsStackFor
        (Presieve.ofArrows X f)) :
    BigHOver.IsZariskiStackInGroupoids B S hS
      (frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration B S hS p hpS) :=
  isZariskiStackInGroupoids_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidFibration B S hS p hpS
    (isStack_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor_zariski B S hS p hpS
      fun U R hRmem ↦ by
        obtain ⟨ι, X, f, rfl⟩ := R.exists_eq_ofArrows
        exact isStackFor_frobeniusVectorBundleGroupoidPseudofunctor B S hS p hpS f
          (hP f hRmem) (hR f hRmem))

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
